---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Cozy Tiny Space"
  description="Cozy Tiny Space helps renters create more storage and organize small apartments without permanent changes — no drilling, no damage, no lost deposit."
  canonicalPath="/about/"
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
    { name: 'About', url: '/about/' },
  ]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 pb-4 pt-10">
    <h1 class="font-display text-[clamp(2rem,5vw,3rem)] font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">About Cozy Tiny Space</h1>
    <div class="article-body mt-6">
      <p>
        <strong>Cozy Tiny Space</strong> helps renters create more storage and organize
        small apartments — without permanent changes. No drilling, no damage, no
        lost deposit.
      </p>
      <p>
        Small apartments are not a storage problem. They are a
        <em>systems</em> problem: the right shelf in the right place, a second
        hanging rod, a hook where you actually reach for your keys. This site
        exists to give renters those systems — measured, tested against rental
        rules, and written so you can do them in an afternoon.
      </p>
      <h2>What this site covers</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Kitchen storage</strong> — pantry, cabinets, countertops and under-sink fixes for rental kitchens.</li>
        <li><strong>Bedroom &amp; closet storage</strong> — wardrobes, under-bed storage and clothing organization without a dresser.</li>
        <li><strong>Bathroom storage</strong> — no-drill shelves, over-toilet storage and under-sink organization for tiny bathrooms.</li>
        <li><strong>Living room &amp; entryway storage</strong> — shoe storage, multifunctional furniture and drop zones with no entryway.</li>
        <li><strong>Renter-friendly solutions</strong> — adhesive hooks, tension rods and removable shelves, with honest weight limits and removal risks.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>What this site does not cover</h2>
      <p>
        We do not cover renovations, permanent installations, or anything that
        needs a landlord's permission to build. We do not publish pure decor
        trends. If a decor idea does not add storage or organization, it does
        not belong here.
      </p>
      <h2>How the guides are written</h2>
      <p>
        Every solution on this site carries the same facts: how much space it
        needs, how it installs, its approximate dimensions, its rental-friendly
        limits, and its pros and cons. Measurements are in inches first, with
        centimetres alongside. Budgets are approximate ranges, not promises.
        Where a product is named, it is a suggestion — not a paid placement.
      </p>
      <h2>Who writes it</h2>
      <p>
        The site is written by <a href="/authors/hamza-hameed/">Hamza Hameed</a>, a
        frontend developer from Karachi, Pakistan, and the founder of
        <a href="https://outfitedits.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener"> Outfit Edits</a>.
        The site is built for readers in the United States first, with the United
        Kingdom, Canada and Australia as secondary audiences.
      </p>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions, corrections or a storage problem we have not covered yet?
        <a href="/contact/"> Get in touch</a> — every message is read.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
